    "body": "## Summary\n- add a configurable platform settlement fee with a 100 bps (1.00%) default\n- snapshot the fee rate when escrow is created so commercial terms never change retroactively\n- keep historical escrow at 0 bps through Flyway V38, preventing retroactive charges\n- settle successful escrow as `gross = platform fee + worker payout` and credit only the worker net amount\n- record platform revenue in a separate idempotent ledger rather than hiding it inside user-wallet mutations\n- persist gross/fee/net settlement breakdown on released escrow with database invariants\n- charge no platform fee on refunds or resumed disputes\n- use the same settlement path for ordinary completion and `RELEASE_TO_WORKER` dispute resolution\n- add current-policy and amount-quote APIs, plus job-specific quotes that use the escrow snapshot and existing job visibility/blocking policy\n- extend finance reconciliation with platform-revenue mismatch detection and accumulated fee revenue\n- show a transparent payout breakdown before publishing a job and before a worker submits/views a proposal\n- add a dedicated 1% platform-fee runtime smoke while preserving the existing wallet-concurrency smoke explicitly at fee=0\n\n## Product policy\nThe default is intentionally low at 1.00% and configurable through `PLATFORM_FEE_BASIS_POINTS`. Product copy does not claim “lowest on the market”. The requester funds only the agreed gross job amount; there is no additional requester surcharge in this slice. The platform fee is recognized only after a successful worker settlement.\n\n## Snapshot semantics\nNew escrow stores `platform_fee_basis_points`. Proposal price adjustments change the gross amount but not the snapshotted rate. Existing-job quote UI reads this snapshot, so changing the global configuration affects only newly-created escrow.\n\n## Accounting\nV38 adds `platform_fee_amount` and `payee_amount` to escrow and creates `platform_revenue_entries`. Release is atomic in the same database transaction: worker wallet credit, platform revenue entry and escrow status/breakdown either commit together or roll back together.\n\n## Validation\n- focused fee rounding/snapshot/service/reconciliation tests\n- legacy Payments ledger smoke runs at 0 bps to isolate concurrency/idempotency behavior\n- new Platform fee settlement smoke runs at 100 bps and verifies 40.00 gross -> 0.40 fee + 39.60 worker payout, refund-without-fee and healthy reconciliation\n- frontend lint/build and full container runtime remain required\n\nDo not merge unless all checks on the latest head are green.",
